# Planted bugs for the RBAC model. Each one must make the named check miss its expectation.
run fv-alloy rbac.als
properties NoEscalationWhenAdminsHoldTheRole NoEscalationWhenAnyoneAdmins
file rbac.als

mutation holding any role is enough to administer every role
detects NoEscalationWhenAdminsHoldTheRole
- pred AdminsHoldTheRole { all u: User | u.admins in u.roles }
+ pred AdminsHoldTheRole { all u: User | some u.admins implies some u.roles }

mutation held permissions also count the roles a user administers
detects NoEscalationWhenAnyoneAdmins
- fun held[u: User]: set Permission { u.roles.perms }
+ fun held[u: User]: set Permission { (u.roles + u.admins).perms }

harmless a comment is reworded
- -- What a user can hand to someone else by adding them to a role.
+ -- The permissions a user can hand to someone else through a role they administer.
